1. Install Minikube
Install Docker (if not already installed)
Shell
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker.io
 
sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo systemctl start docker
 
docker --version

Add your user to Docker group:

Shell
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker
Install kubectl
Shell
curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
 
chmod +x kubectl
 
sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/
 
kubectl version --client
Install Minikube
Shell
curl -LO https://storage.googleapis.com/minikube/releases/latest/minikube-linux-amd64
 
sudo install minikube-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/minikube
 
minikube version
2. Start Minikube

Using Docker driver:

Shell
minikube start --driver=docker

Verify:

Shell
kubectl get nodes

Expected:

Shell
NAME STATUS ROLES AGE
minikube Ready control-plane 2m
3. Create Multiple Pods
Method 1: Deployment (Recommended)

Create nginx-deploy.yaml

YAML
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
name: nginx-deployment
 
spec:
replicas: 3
 
selector:
matchLabels:
app: nginx
 
template:
metadata:
labels:
app: nginx
 
spec:
containers:
- name: nginx
image: nginx:latest
ports:
- containerPort: 80

Deploy:

Shell
kubectl apply -f nginx-deploy.yaml

Check pods:

Shell
kubectl get pods

Output:

Shell
NAME READY STATUS
nginx-deployment-xxxx1 1/1 Running
nginx-deployment-xxxx2 1/1 Running
nginx-deployment-xxxx3 1/1 Running
 
4. Scale Pods

Increase to 5 pods:

Shell
kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5

Verify:

Shell
kubectl get pods
5. Expose Deployment

Create service:

Shell
kubectl expose deployment nginx-deployment \
--type=NodePort \
--port=80

Check service:

Shell
kubectl get svc

Open application:

Shell
minikube service nginx-deployment
6. Useful Commands
List all pods
Shell
kubectl get pods
List deployments
Shell
kubectl get deployments
List services
Shell
kubectl get svc
Describe pod
Shell
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
Pod logs
Shell
kubectl logs <pod-name>
Delete deployment
Shell
kubectl delete deployment nginx-deployment
Example for Learning Kubernetes

Deploy 5 Nginx Pods:

Shell
kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx
 
kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=5
 
kubectl get pods

This is the simplest way to practice Kubernetes concepts such as Pods → ReplicaSets → Deployments → Services on your Ubuntu VM before moving to a full cluster with kubeadm, EKS, AKS, or GKE.

